The Elders are the ruling body of [[Geography/Althane/Brejvasing/index|Brejvasing]], drawn from the largest families in the Leviathan. The council, also called the Seed of Elders, meets in [[Geography/Althane/Brejvasing/Kryperkyst|Kryperkyst]], and since the country's founding has kept a strict isolationist policy to keep the Leviathan's secrets from outsiders.

The Elders have been dead for a long time. Each embedded a piece of their spirit in the arcane machinery built into the seats at the end of a long bridge, and only a few surface at a time, so a visitor finds a different handful awake on any given day. The current head is [[People/Althane/Zora|Zora]], an [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Aphorite|aphorite]] dwarf; another seat holds a hydrin, a gilled merfolk whose long robes trail into the floor because his body is not really there. An Elder's mouth moves a half-second before the sound of their voice arrives.
